            "question": "What does a Boca Raton HOA architectural committee want to see for a glass railing?",
            "answer": "<p>Committees usually ask for a site plan or photo showing where the railing goes, the height, the hardware finish and the product specifications. Our product pages give panel heights and spigot dimensions. The engineering and testing page covers attachments on concrete and wood, and the sample kit shows the actual glass and both finishes. Get the committee's approval in writing first, then apply for the city permit.</p>",
